nagisa-rs

The Rust implementation was extracted from aligner-rust-ja in
fishaudio/apex-fish-inference PR #84, at commit
46879e4b0d8224019f1a6f39e62baa3d599a8de4:
https://github.com/fishaudio/apex-fish-inference/pull/84
https://github.com/fishaudio/apex-fish-inference/tree/46879e4b0d8224019f1a6f39e62baa3d599a8de4/aligner-rust/crates/aligner-rust-ja
Its workspace declares the Apache License, Version 2.0, retained here.
Standalone packaging, documentation, examples and maintenance tools were
adapted for this repository; the segmentation algorithm is retained.

This is a port of the word-segmentation component of nagisa 0.2.11,
originally implemented in Python/Cython using DyNet by Taishi Ikeda
(taishi-i) and contributors:
https://github.com/taishi-i/nagisa
https://pypi.org/project/nagisa/0.2.11/
Copyright (c) 2018 taishi-i
The upstream MIT license is reproduced in licenses/nagisa-MIT.txt.
The pretrained dictionary and model are supplied separately by nagisa;
they are not bundled in this repository or the Rust package.

Unicode normalization and casing tables were generated from CPython
3.12.14 (Unicode 15.0.0). The Unicode data license is reproduced in
licenses/Unicode-3.0.txt.
